This is a collection of YANIs by users of the #nethack IRC channel on
freenode.net. Please excuse any old ideas that may be present.

[2]: A party hat. Putting it on welds it to your head. "You suddenly
realize it's your birthday today!" Applying and extinguishing a candle
will prompt you for a wish then destroy both the hat and candle. One
more candle will be neccesary on subsequent attempts. --Patashu

[3]: Actually it should be a number of candles equal to your xp level,
and it should only be a slight chance of a wish (most people don't get
their birthday wishes, do they?) --BenUrban

[4]: If you dig a hole on a level that is illuminated which comes out
on a level that is not, there should be a small illuminated region on
the dark level where you fall through to. --azgor

[5]: If you throw a cream pie at a monster that is in posession of a
cream pie, that monster should always retaliate initially by throwing
its pie. --azgor

[6]: Applying or wearing a towel while equipmentless in a steam vortex
should produce a YAFM. "Boy, it feels like a sauna in here!" --Patashu

[7]: If you attempt to dig a hole and you have fumbling and "Your swing
misses its mark." you should hit yourself in the foot, injuring your
leg and taking damage. --azgor

[8]: Why just wands of nothing? Rings of nothing and amulets of nothing
too. That way every class of item has something 'useless' in it.
--Patashu

[9]: I just found a burnt copper wand in a bones pile; that shouldn't
happen. --BenUrban

[10]: Golems should fuse with items of their own kind for a small HP
bonus per object and drop them when killed. "The iron golem welds a
long sword to its body!" --Patashu

[11]: putting a BoH or wand of cancellation into a BoH destroys the bag
as usual, and additionally creates a magic portal to the BagZone, where
you can quest to reclaim your lost items. "as you put a bag inside, you
are blasted by a magical explosion! You tear a hole in space-time!"
--magicalblender

[12]: YAOI(?): You can change gender, you can change allignment, and
you can change race. There should be a way to change class. Maybe make
it a one time only event. Also, if you should ascend, there should be
something to indicate that you switched classes in the logs. That way
you won't get full credit for a true monk ascension if you only ever
did the valkyrie quest. --azgor

[13]: Maybe be able to name potions of booze in the options file, like
the slime mold. --ilya86

[14]: attacking energy vortexes (and other shock critters) with a
non-metal weapon shouldn't give you shock damage --Botje


